.TH CLIPDECK 1 "November 2026" "Clipdeck 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clipdeck \- clipboard history manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clipdeck
[\fB\-\-show\fR | \fB\-\-paste\fR \fIN\fR | \fB\-\-paste\-plain\fR | \fB\-\-save\fR | \fB\-\-background\fR | \fB\-\-quit\fR | \fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Clipdeck keeps a searchable history of everything you copy. It runs in the
system tray; press its keyboard shortcut (Ctrl+` by default) to open the
history, type to search, and press Enter to paste.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B (none)
Start Clipdeck, or open the history if it is already running.
.TP
.B \-\-show
Open the history window. Bind this to a keyboard shortcut.
.TP
.BI \-\-paste " N"
Paste clip number \fIN\fR (1 is the top of the history, counting pinned clips first).
.TP
.B \-\-paste\-plain
Paste what is on the clipboard as plain text.
.TP
.B \-\-save
Save what is on the clipboard now, even while capturing is paused.
.TP
.B \-\-background
Start without showing anything if Clipdeck isn't running (used at login).
.TP
.B \-\-quit
Stop the running instance.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/clipdeck/clips.db
Clipboard history.
.TP
.I ~/.config/clipdeck/clipdeck.conf
Settings, including the sync passphrase.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CLIPDECK_QT
Set to \fBpyside6\fR or \fBpyqt6\fR to choose the Qt binding.
.SH AUTHOR
Farroukh Artikov
